kind: exclusive
reason: solar2_dump runs the PAI tree on 32 CPU threads and maps the fixture through the CPU backend; beside a timed run or a gate batch
  it would take their cores and their memory bandwidth, so it holds the lease; why now: the fixture tier's oracle sets that
  gate_solar2_e2e's layer_outputs_near_pai_fx reads, without which the gate ends by name before the card loads (round qsolfx)
